    "float4_note": "The vector path's lexical prior derives from ts_rank_cd, which returns float4, so it crosses the wire as the shortest decimal that round-trips to a float4 rather than as the exact value the SQL multiplied by 0.10. That caps the reproducible precision of the lexical term at about 6e-8, i.e. about 6e-9 of the final score at weight 0.10, and it is the entire reason worst_absolute_error sits above double-precision noise — it is one row in 48,000, the only rows affected being the handful where the lexical prior is non-zero at all. Keyword mode ranks with BM25, a float8 expression, so its lexical prior round-trips exactly and the float4 reconstruction makes it WORSE there; that is why worst_absolute_error_float4_adjusted is larger than worst_absolute_error for keyword mode and smaller for semantic mode. worst_absolute_error_best_representation reads each row in the width its own SQL used and is the honest residual: double-precision noise. Semantic, citation and recency priors are float8 throughout and round-trip exactly.",
